_cefore_notice() {
    cat <<'NOTICE'
Cefore does not ship a key pair. Generate one before starting cefnetd:

  sudo openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -out /etc/cefore/default-private-key
  sudo openssl rsa -pubout -in /etc/cefore/default-private-key \
       -out /etc/cefore/default-public-key
  sudo chmod 600 /etc/cefore/default-private-key

cefnetd and ccninfo read the private key, so run them as root
(e.g. sudo cefnetdstart, sudo ccninfo ...).

cefnetdstart prints nothing when cefnetd fails to start. Check
/tmp/cefnetd_<port>_0.log (default: /tmp/cefnetd_9695_0.log).

CCNINFO_VALID_ALG=rsa-sha256 additionally needs
/etc/cefore/.ccninfo/ccninfo_rt-{private,public}-key and
~/.ccninfo/ccninfo_user-{private,public}-key.

To use csmgrd (or conpubd) as the Content Store, set CS_MODE=2 (or 3)
in /etc/cefore/cefnetd.conf, and start csmgrd before cefnetd.

csmgrd needs larger socket buffers. Example tuning is in
/usr/share/doc/cefore/88-cefore.conf:
  Apply until reboot:  sudo sysctl -p /usr/share/doc/cefore/88-cefore.conf
  Apply permanently:   copy it to /etc/sysctl.d/ and run sudo sysctl --system
NOTICE
}

post_install() {
    _cefore_notice
}

post_upgrade() {
    [ -f /etc/cefore/default-private-key ] && return
    _cefore_notice
}
